  "result": "Perfect! All 234 tests pass. The VAT summary report feature is now fully implemented and tested. Here's what was added:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Added `vatSummary(invoices)` to `src/reports.js`**:\n   - Filters invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n   - Groups line items by VAT rate\n   - For each VAT rate, calculates:\n     - base: sum of (lineTotal - lineDiscount) for all lines at that rate\n     - vat: sum of lineVAT for all lines at that rate\n   - Returns array of { rate, base, vat }\n   - Sorted by rate descending (21%, 9%, 0%)\n\n2. **Key Features:**\n   - Accurate base calculation (after line discounts)\n   - Proper VAT aggregation by rate\n   - Filters by invoice status correctly\n   - Handles multiple VAT rates in single invoice\n   - Aggregates across multiple invoices\n   - Zero-rate VAT items included with vat: 0\n   - Handles tier discounts properly\n   - Respects all invoice modifiers\n\n3. **Comprehensive test suite** with 16 tests in `test/reports.test.js` covering:\n   - Empty invoice list\n   - Single VAT rate\n   - Multiple VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n   - Sorting by rate descending\n   - Base calculation with discounts\n   - VAT calculation accuracy\n   - Draft invoice exclusion\n   - Partially paid invoice inclusion\n   - Paid invoice inclusion\n   - Multiple invoice aggregation\n   - Applied discount handling\n   - Zero-rate VAT items\n   - Mixed VAT rates and amounts\n   - Tier discount application\n   - VAT-exempt and regular items\n   - Zero VAT for 0% rate\n\nThe VAT summary report provides tax compliance and audit support, breaking down taxable bases and tax amounts by rate for all active invoices.",
